PhotoFlow — End User Licence Agreement
Samiksha Technologies

Version 1.0 — 5 August 2026

IMPORTANT: This is a draft prepared for the beta release. Have it reviewed by a
lawyer qualified in Indian law before you charge money for this software. It is
written to be clear and fair rather than exhaustive, and it is not legal advice.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. AGREEMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This agreement is between you (either an individual or the organisation you
represent) and Samiksha Technologies ("we", "us"). By installing or using
PhotoFlow ("the Software") you accept these terms. If you do not accept them,
do not install or use the Software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. LICENCE GRANTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and use the
Software as follows.

2.1  Trial. You may evaluate the Software free of charge for the trial period
     shown in the application. No payment or licence key is required during the
     trial.

2.2  Beta. While the Software is marked as a beta release it is provided free of
     charge. We may change or end the beta at any time, with reasonable notice.

2.3  Licensed use. Once you hold a valid licence key, you may install and use the
     Software on the number of computers your licence permits. Unless stated
     otherwise, one licence covers two computers used by the same person.

2.4  Your work is yours. Every photograph, album, print sheet, collage and other
     output you create with the Software belongs entirely to you. We claim no
     rights over it and there are no restrictions on its commercial use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
You may not:

  (a) share, resell, rent or sublicense the Software or your licence key;
  (b) use one licence key on more computers than it permits;
  (c) attempt to remove or bypass the licensing, trial or activation mechanisms;
  (d) decompile or reverse-engineer the Software, except where law expressly
      permits it despite a term such as this;
  (e) remove or alter any copyright or ownership notices.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. YOUR PHOTOGRAPHS AND YOUR PRIVACY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1  The Software processes your photographs on your own computer. We do not
     receive, upload, store or have any access to them.

4.2  Licensing. When you activate a licence key, the Software sends us the key
     and an anonymous identifier derived from your computer's hardware, so we can
     confirm the licence and count installations. It contains nothing that
     identifies you or your clients.

4.3  Optional usage statistics. If, and only if, you choose to enable it, the
     Software may send counts of how often each tool is used, along with the
     application version and your operating system version. It never includes
     photographs, file names, folder names, client details or anything you have
     typed. You can see exactly what would be sent from within the application,
     and you may turn it off at any time, which also deletes what was collected.

4.4  Your rights. You may ask us what data we hold about you, ask us to correct
     or delete it, or withdraw your consent to usage statistics. Write to the
     address in section 10.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. OWNERSHIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software is licensed, not sold. Samiksha Technologies retains all
intellectual property rights in it. This agreement gives you no rights to our
trade marks or branding.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software includes open-source components, each under its own licence,
including but not limited to: Python, Qt (PyQt6), OpenCV, NumPy, Pillow,
MediaPipe, SciPy and psd-tools. Those licences continue to apply to those
components, and where they grant you rights that this agreement would otherwise
restrict, their terms prevail for that component. A full list of components and
licences is available on request.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. NO WARRANTY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular
purpose, or non-infringement.

You are responsible for keeping backups of your photographs. The Software is
designed never to modify or delete your original files, but no software is free
of defects and no backup strategy should depend on that.

Automated results — including photograph selection, quality scoring, face
detection, person grouping, cropping and layout — are suggestions produced by
software and will not always be correct. Review the output before delivering it
to a client.

The Software helps you produce photographs at sizes you specify. It does not
certify that any photograph will be accepted for a passport, visa, identity
document or any other purpose. Confirm the current official requirements
yourself.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect,
incidental, special or consequential loss, or for lost profits, lost business or
lost or corrupted data, arising from your use of or inability to use the
Software.

Our total liability under this agreement will not exceed the amount you paid us
for the Software in the twelve months before the claim arose, or ₹1,000 if you
paid nothing.

Nothing in this agreement excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. TERM AND TERMINATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This agreement applies for as long as you use the Software. It ends
automatically if you materially breach it, in which case you must stop using the
Software and remove it from your computers. You may end it at any time by
uninstalling the Software. Sections 4, 5, 7 and 8 survive termination.

